[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Mutilated Ladies]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.24]Lesson 7 | 第7课
[00:01.89]Mutilated Ladies | 残钞鉴定组
[00:08.69]Why did Jane cook John's wallet? | 简为什么把约翰的钱包煮了？
[00:12.78]Has it ever happened to you? | 这种事在你身上发生过吗？
[00:15.17]Have you ever put your trousers in the washing machine and then remembered there was a large bank note in your back pocket? | 你有没有把裤子放进洗衣机、然后才想起后兜里有一张大面额钞票的经历？
[00:23.29]When you rescued your trousers, did you find the note was whiter than white? | 把裤子抢救出来时，你是否发现纸币已白得不能再白了？
[00:29.10]People who live in Britain needn't despair when they make mistakes like this (and a lot of people do)! | 在英国，人们犯了这样的错误不必绝望（许多人常犯这种错误）！
[00:36.62]Fortunately for them, the Bank of England has a team called Mutilated Ladies | 幸运的是，英格兰银行有一个叫“残钞鉴定组”的部门，
[00:42.32]which deals with claims from people who fed their money to a machine or to their dog. | 专门处理那些把钱喂进机器或者喂了狗的人提出的索赔要求。
[00:48.62]Dogs, it seems, love to chew up money! | 看来，狗很喜欢咀嚼钞票！
[00:52.94]A recent case concerns Jane Butlin whose fiance, John, runs a successful furniture business. | 最近的一个案例与简·巴特林有关，她的未婚夫约翰经营着一家生意红火的家具店。
[01:01.06]John had a very good day and put his wallet containing ￡3, 000 into the microwave oven for safekeeping. | 那天约翰生意很好，他把一只装有3000英镑的钱包放进微波炉里保存。
[01:09.99]Then he and Jane went horse-riding. | 然后他和简一起去骑马。
[01:12.63]When they got home, Jane cooked their dinner in the microwave oven and without realizing it, cooked her fiance's wallet as well. | 回家后，简用微波炉煮晚饭，无意之中把她未婚夫的钱包也一起煮了。
[01:22.99]Imagine their dismay when they found a beautifully-cooked wallet and notes turned to ash! | 想象一下他们发现一只煮得漂漂亮亮的钱包和化为灰烬的钞票时的沮丧心情吧！
[01:31.09]John went to see his bank manager who sent the remains of wallet and the money | 约翰去找银行经理，经理把钱包的残片和钞票
[01:36.68]to the special department of the Bank of England in Newcastle: the Mutilated Ladies! | 寄到了英格兰银行在纽卡斯尔的专门部门：残钞鉴定组！
[01:42.82]They examined the remains and John got all his money back. | 他们对残片进行了鉴别，约翰取回了全部钱款。
[01:48.33]'So long as there's something to identify, we will give people their money back,' said a spokeswoman for the Bank. | “只要有可供辨认的东西，我们就会把钱退还给人，”银行的一位女发言人说。
[01:56.56]'Last year, we paid ￡1.5 million on 21,000 claims.' | “去年，我们对2.1万起索赔支付了150万英镑。”
